# Project overlay — YOURS. The scaffold creates this file once and never
# overwrites it.
#
# Most of model/ is toolchain-derived and is deliberately regenerated so that
# toolchain fixes propagate; this file, the guide, and the target, feature and
# edition indexes are kept. Put anything here that is a decision about THIS
# project rather than a fact about the API.
#
# Included LAST by sdk.aontu, after target/target-index.aontu, because a key
# under main.kit.target.<t> can only refine a target that has already been
# defined. Declared earlier, the model build fails with "Cannot unify value:
# nil with value: string / key ext value was: nil", which names nothing that
# would lead you here.
#
# The release version each generated manifest declares (package.json,
# pyproject.toml, the gemspec, the rockspec) and that the port Makefiles tag:
#
#   main: kit: target: ts: publish: version: '1.2.3'
#
# Per target, because ports publish to different registries on different
# clocks. Set every target to the same value for a lockstep repo.
#
# A published package name that does not follow the derivation:
#
#   main: kit: target: ts: publish: registry: package: '@scope/name'

main: kit: publisher: {
  name: 'Yele Zhong'
  url: 'https://github.com/DEOWL-kan'
}

main: kit: repo: path: 'DEOWL-kan/spaceflight-news-sdk'

main: kit: target: ts: publish: registry: package: 'spaceflight-news-sdk'

main: kit: text: {
  homepage: 'https://spaceflightnewsapi.net'
  docs_url: 'https://api.spaceflightnewsapi.net/v4/docs/'
  about_md: `
An unofficial TypeScript SDK for the [Spaceflight News API](https://spaceflightnewsapi.net) (SNAPI) v4, generated with the [Voxgig SDK Generator](https://voxgig.com/sdk). No API key is needed.

**Run the example** (Node.js 24 LTS):

\`\`\`bash
cd ts && npm install && npm run build && cd ..
node examples/list-articles.ts
\`\`\`

**Regenerate** from the live spec:

\`\`\`bash
cd .sdk && npm install
node build/fetch-def.mjs   # writes def/snapi.json
npm run generate           # writes ../ts
\`\`\`

\`fetch-def.mjs\` keeps the spec's interface (paths, parameters, schemas) and drops its prose (\`description\`, \`example\`), because the spec text carries no stated license. The spec itself is not committed, so \`.sdk/def/\` is empty until you run the script.

**Attribution.** SNAPI is run by [The Space Devs](https://thespacedevs.com); its articles, blogs and reports are aggregated from third-party publishers and belong to them. The MIT license here covers this repository's own code only; the generator templates are Voxgig's, see [THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md](THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md).
`
}
